<comment>
Bai & Stone 2011 (ApJ 736, 144) -- Section 2.3.2: Damping of MHD Waves
1D, fast magnetosonic wave, rightgoing (wave_flag=6 for ideal-gas 7-mode eigensystem)

Background: same as bs11_alfven.  vf = 2.0, vs = 0.5

Analytic damping rate (eq. 17):
  Gamma_f = (1/2) * (vf^2 - cs^2)/(vf^2 - vs^2) * k^2*vA^2 / omega_a
          = (1/2) * (4-1)/(4-0.25) * 4*pi^2*(13/4) / 100
          = (1/2) * (3/3.75) * 13*pi^2/100
          = 5.2*pi^2/100  ~= 0.513

tlim: actual_tlim = tlim_input * (lx / eigenvalue)
  For fast (eigenvalue = vf = 2.0): actual_tlim = 10.0 * (1.0/2.0) = 5.0 --> run to t=5

<job>
basename  = fast_1d

<problem>
pgen_name = linear_wave
wave_flag = 6         # rightgoing fast wave: eigenvalue[6] = v1 + cf = 0+2 = 2.0
amp       = 1.0e-4
dens      = 1.0
pgas      = 0.6
bx0       = 1.0
by0       = 1.41421356237309504
bz0       = 0.5
along_x1  = true

<mesh>
nghost    = 2
nx1       = 32
x1min     = 0.0
x1max     = 1.0
ix1_bc    = periodic
ox1_bc    = periodic
nx2       = 1
x2min     = 0.0
x2max     = 1.0
ix2_bc    = periodic
ox2_bc    = periodic
nx3       = 1
x3min     = 0.0
x3max     = 1.0
ix3_bc    = periodic
ox3_bc    = periodic

<meshblock>
nx1 = 32

<time>
evolution  = dynamic
integrator = rk2
cfl_number = 0.4
tlim       = 10.0    # actual_tlim = 10.0 * (1.0/2.0) = 5.0 code units

<mhd>
eos                 = ideal
gamma               = 1.6666666666666667
reconstruct         = plm
rsolver             = hlld
ambipolar_diffusion = 0.0325

<output1>
file_type   = tab
variable    = mhd_bcc
data_format = %14.8e
dt          = 0.1
slice_x2    = 0.0
slice_x3    = 0.0
